+# ── hard wall-clock deadline (self-terminating watchdog) ───────────
+# The CFN CreationPolicy timeout only stops WAITING; it does not stop the GPU.
+# Every path that ends this script normally -- success, die(), the ERR trap --
+# depends on the script still running, so a hung eval or a wedged apt lock bills
+# g6.xlarge until a human notices. This watchdog is a separate process whose only
+# job is to outlive that failure: it sleeps a fixed budget, then terminates the
+# instance itself via the EC2 API. It is armed BEFORE install (the hang can
+# happen there too) and disarmed by PID kill on the normal exit paths.
+#
+# Deliberately not `shutdown -h`: an instance stopped rather than terminated can
+# keep billing EBS, and shutdown depends on a healthy init the hang may have taken
+# out. Terminating from the API side needs nothing from this box but the network.
+LANG_DEADLINE_MIN={{ lang_deadline_minutes }}
+log "  [watchdog] arming hard deadline: ${LANG_DEADLINE_MIN} min from now"
+# The watchdog records its OWN pid rather than relying on $! -- `setsid` may or may
+# not fork depending on whether the caller is already a process-group leader, so $!
+# is not reliably the sleeping shell. Disarming the wrong pid would leave an armed
+# timer that terminates a healthy instance mid-run.
